  "definition": "Ehlers' average whose factor exp(-4.6 x (D - 1)) follows the fractal dimension D of the high-low ranges of the last two period windows.",
  "boundaries": "Written from MetaTrader's help formula, starting at the close of the first full window; MetaQuotes' own code may seed it differently.",
  "recognition": "Price above a rising FrAMA reads as up, below a falling one as down.",
